Input: {"question": "What is the location of Mooretown?", "original_source_segments": {"D1S1": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0179-e2c76fabf992:d00", "start": 0, "end": 167, "text": "Moore Town, Jamaica Moore Town is a Maroon settlement located in the Blue Mountains and John Crow Mountains of Portland, Jamaica, accessible by road from Port Antonio."}, "D1S2": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0179-e2c76fabf992:d00", "start": 168, "end": 252, "text": "The easternmost Maroon town, Moore Town is located in the eastern end of the parish."}, "D1S3": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0179-e2c76fabf992:d00", "start": 253, "end": 417, "text": "Formerly known as New Nanny Town, Moore Town was founded in 1740 when the Peace Treaty was signed between the British colonial authorities and the Windward Maroons."}, "D1S4": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0179-e2c76fabf992:d00", "start": 418, "end": 507, "text": "This treaty allotted the Moore Town Maroons 1000 acres, but Moore Town only received 500."}, "D1S5": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0179-e2c76fabf992:d00", "start": 508, "end": 580, "text": "In 1781 the initial 500 acres was augmented with another 500-1270 acres."}, "D1S6": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0179-e2c76fabf992:d00", "start": 581, "end": 602, "text": "While Maroons and the"}, "D2S1": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0179-e2c76fabf992:d01", "start": 0, "end": 167, "text": "Mooretown Rancheria of Maidu Indians The Mooretown Rancheria of Maidu Indians of California is a federally recognized tribe of Concow and Maidu people in Butte County."}, "D2S2": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0179-e2c76fabf992:d01", "start": 168, "end": 360, "text": "Concow, or Konkow, people are the northwestern or foothill branch of the Maidu people, who traditionally spoke the Concow language Mooretown Rancheria is headquartered in Oroville, California."}, "D2S3": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0179-e2c76fabf992:d01", "start": 361, "end": 476, "text": "The tribe is governed by a democratically elected, tribal council, and the current tribal chairperson is Ben Clark."}, "D2S4": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0179-e2c76fabf992:d01", "start": 477, "end": 563, "text": "The Mooretown Rancheria is a federally recognized ranchería with an area of 109 acres."}, "D2S5": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0179-e2c76fabf992:d01", "start": 564, "end": 634, "text": "It is located in the community of Oroville East, in suburban Oroville."}, "D2S6": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0179-e2c76fabf992:d01", "start": 635, "end": 659, "text": "Other nearby communities"}, "D3S1": {"document_number": 3, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0179-e2c76fabf992:d02", "start": 0, "end": 54, "text": "F��dϪ\u0003�CG� ɐ\u0002�a0�\u0000 ] � > �I����A� # ����U�M.レ߰ > �j� ?"}, "D3S2": {"document_number": 3, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0179-e2c76fabf992:d02", "start": 55, "end": 69, "text": "Z\u0016��f� { ��� ?"}, "D3S3": {"document_number": 3, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0179-e2c76fabf992:d02", "start": 70, "end": 150, "text": "W\b/Cy @ �� \u0013�t��u�P� ; K1�e\u001b�\u000fx������\u0017���\u000f ] 5��Zn�'L5���Q�+��\u0018��h�\u000fR� # ��\u0017\u0003� !"}, "D3S4": {"document_number": 3, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0179-e2c76fabf992:d02", "start": 151, "end": 343, "text": "~\b�v34��ri6� �\u000e��c��t� ) ; VK_��\u000f� > X\u0006�B� G_ZA��\u0006/x�Y\u001b�/���� Ě� ` � % ����������4 [ ���C\u000fx�D� �װ\u000eV� & ( e�\u0001�_\u0007\u001aE� ` @ \u000fH�d�j�� a�L�x�d�\u0015��QO���īʻ2t�ܭr�9��� , �I\u000f���bmQƱ����k��u� } ���� [ � ?"}, "D3S5": {"document_number": 3, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0179-e2c76fabf992:d02", "start": 344, "end": 544, "text": "�2��͠�şx\u0019��\u0001�sـ��Щ�Բ�u����Ce��T�u * �� : Do4T���R�'�F��� * � ; ���Ԑ ��ͺ��q { �1u\u0011��I�҃�Ƌ~ & \u0012��T^H=�.s��� : �i �����5��c�k� # �� `` ߝ���rC�|x�ޥI�� ( ��\u0005�Is�\u00189���/�t����UX�o��� : .�GǙ # ��� : r �\u001b\u0001�u !"}, "D3S6": {"document_number": 3, "doc_id"